[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The merge boundary is not a joint

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-SEMANTIC-LAYER-GAP-MERGE-BOUNDARY-IS-NOT-A-JOINT
TITLE: The merge boundary is not a joint
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: prose
PLACE: screen
STATEMENT: >>>
nix flake check is the only gate nobody can bypass, and it appears in neither list of joints. Merge and rewrite fire only after the fact. So every rule that belongs at merge time — the fingerprint check on the merge ref, plan-reference checks, catching authorship changes (an AUTHORED_BY flip), severity by joint — has nowhere to attach.

> The merge boundary is not a joint: nix flake check is the only unbypassable gate and appears in neither joint list, git.merge|rewrite are post-only, so every merge-time rule (fp-check on the merge ref, plan refs, flip detection, per-joint severity) has nowhere to attach.
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
DEC-LONG-LIVED-BRANCH:0000000
INV-NO-EXTERNAL-PLAN-REFS:0000000
MECH-FP-MAIN-LINEAGE:0000000
